DESCRIPTION:Looking for a fun and educational activity for your littlest s
 ailor? Join us on Fridays at 10:30 for Lake Champlain Maritime Museum’s 
 weekly storytime! Families with young children (recommended age 5 and youn
 ger) are invited to gather with a Museum educator in our historic summer c
 amp building\, the Roost\, as we read some of our favorite stories about L
 ake Champlain and summer adventures on the water out loud for all to enjoy
 . Stories will be read as a group and there will also be coloring pages an
 d crafts available afterwards. Storytime meets every Friday from May 29–
 October 16. This program is free to attend with no registration required. 
 The Roost is situated off of a gravel path at the back of the Museum green
 . The ramp at the back of the building is accessible over grass. There is 
 a high threshold at the entrance of the ramp. For accessibility requests p
 lease contact us by email at info@lcmm.org or by phone at 802-475-2022. Ev
 ery week through Oct 16\, 2026. 4472 Basin Harbor Road Vergennes \, Vermon
 t 05491 802-475-2022 info@lcmm.org https://www.lcmm.org/ Submit An Event F
 ind out what's happening in your neck of the woods with Vermont Public's f
 ree Events newsletter. Email Address * Editorial Emails Breaking News | se
 nt occasionally The Frequency | Daily News Update\, sent weekday mornings 
 Capitol Recap | Vermont Legislature Wrap\, sent Fridays during the session
  Brave Little State | People-Powered Journalism\, sent every other Saturda
 y But Why | A Podcast For Curious Kids\, sent every other Friday Homegoing
 s | A righteous space for art and race\, sent bi-weekly following an episo
 de drop Out There | Out There | Your monthly dose of the environment + the
  great outdoors\, sent Thursday mor Supporter Emails Membership Renewal No
 tices | Sent 12 months after your most recent contribution The President's
  Report | A letter from our president exclusively for members of our Produ
 cers Circle The Transmitter | A behind-the-scenes newsletter exclusively f
 or active members\, sent the first Tues But Why Fan Club | Activity Newsle
 tter exclusively for active members of the But Why Fan Club\, sent Other F
 undraising Emails | Matching challenges\, prize drawings and more\, sent p
 eriodically Audience Emails Program Schedules | Full TV listings for all c
 hannels\, sent monthly This Week | Weekly program highlights\, sent each w
 eekend Events | Upcoming Vermont Public events\, sent occasionally Station
  Updates | Sent occasionally Recently Added 'The Foreigner' by Larry Shue 
 'The Foreigner' by Larry Shue A Living Song Barr Hill Wild Culture Ferment
